Z||000000||86seyellow||06-11-2001||10:31 AM||||I need to know where I can find out if my SE has had nay of the recalls done. There are zero campaign stickers anywhere and by looking at it according to a 2.8 without the recall on the throttle body it appears no work has ever been done.<P>Please<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-11-2001||10:50 AM||||Check on the inside of your fuel filler door, there should be a "check and change oil frequently" sticker in there.<P>Also, part of the recall was to remove a piece of weatherstrip that goes between the rear decklid and the back window.  This was removed to let more air out.  If it's not there, it's probably been done.  You'll see some holes where it was attached.<P>Also, keep in mind that though your car has had the service done to it, the dealership that did it might have forgotten to attach the correct labels.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||86seyellow||06-11-2001||10:52 AM||||the weatherstrip is there between the deck and back window, kinda like flanges. no stickers anywhere<P>\<BR>HELP<BR>||||reg||1
